        "title": {
          "en": "OpenAI to Honor Robots.txt for AI Training Preferences",
          "zh": "OpenAI 将遵守 robots.txt 信号以管理 AI 训练偏好"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "OpenAI announced it will respect a shared robots.txt signal to allow website operators to communicate their AI training preferences to participating providers.",
          "zh": "OpenAI 宣布将遵守共享的 robots.txt 信号，以帮助网站运营者向参与的提供商传达其 AI 训练偏好。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "OpenAI commits to honoring a shared robots.txt signal.",
            "The signal enables website operators to communicate their AI training preferences.",
            "This system is designed for use with 'participating providers,' indicating potential industry-wide adoption."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "OpenAI 承诺遵守共享的 robots.txt 信号。",
            "该信号使网站运营者能够传达其 AI 训练偏好。",
            "此系统旨在与“参与的提供商”配合使用，表明可能在行业内推广。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This development establishes a standardized mechanism for content creators to control how their data is used by AI models, potentially influencing the scope and source of future AI training datasets. It marks an industry move towards greater transparency and user control over data usage in AI development.",
          "zh": "这一进展为内容创建者建立了标准化机制，以控制其数据如何被 AI 模型使用，可能影响未来 AI 训练数据集的范围和来源。这标志着 AI 发展中，行业正走向更高的透明度和用户对数据使用权的控制。"
        },
        "source": "OpenAI News",
        "link": "https://openai.com/index/helping-websites-express-ai-training-preferences"
      },
